# CodeProbe project-mode exclusion template
#
# Copy this file to `.codeprobeignore` at the root of a student project when
# using Open project ZIP, Open folder or the native project analyser.
#
# Supported subset: comments, blank lines, directory patterns ending in `/`,
# glob patterns such as `*.min.js`, anchored patterns beginning with `/`, and
# negation with `!` for files that must be re-included.
# A slash within a pattern makes it project-root-relative; a leading `/` also
# anchors a basename. A trailing `/` marks directories without anchoring the
# pattern. Use `**/` explicitly to match deeper paths.
# Native folder intake reads the bounded root and explicit rules before it
# chooses subtrees to expand. A fixed-prefix negation reopens only compatible
# subtrees. A basename or leading-wildcard negation may require wider traversal,
# still bounded by the entry limit and a maximum directory depth of 64.
# Unexpanded directories are reported separately: their children were not read
# or counted as inspected files. Negation never bypasses path or byte limits.

# Dependencies and vendor code
node_modules/
bower_components/
vendor/
vendors/
third_party/
third-party/
external/
lib/
libs/
packages/

# Generated, compiled or build output
dist/
build/
out/
target/
bin/
obj/
coverage/
htmlcov/
site/
.next/
generated/
gen/
autogen/
auto_generated/
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.bundle.js
*.map
*.class
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Python environments and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.pyc

# Framework or package-manager locks that students normally do not author
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
poetry.lock
Pipfile.lock
Cargo.lock

# Data, assets and media
*.csv
*.json
*.xml
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.svg
*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx
*.xlsx

# Documentation and assignment prose; project mode excludes these by default,
# but listing them here makes the policy explicit and visible to students.
README.md
docs/
*.md
*.rst
*.adoc
*.docx
*.pdf

# Instructor starter code or scaffold folders - rename for your module.
starter/
template/
scaffold/
provided/
instructor/

# Tests may be student-authored. Exclude only if your course does not assess them.
# tests/

# Example re-inclusion rule: if a generated-looking folder contains a file the
# student actually authored, exclude the folder first and re-include that file.
# This is root-relative. It does not re-include a nested dependency copy.
# generated/
# !generated/student_owned.py
